      "body_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So this is the convert of</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"impl Default for VmSpace {\n    fn default() -&gt; Self {\n        Self::new()\n    }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">impl</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">Default</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">for</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">VmSpace</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">default</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> -&gt; <span class=\"pl-smi\">Self</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">Self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span><span class=\"pl-en\">new</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rikosellic/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rikosellic\">@rikosellic</a> Shall we add a comment of the original code to infer that there is a convertion?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Well, there could be two ways:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Convert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.</li>\n<li>Use <code class=\"notranslate\">ExTrait</code> and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for <code class=\"notranslate\">ExDefault</code> that forbids us to declare another one</p>",
      "body_text": "So this is the convert of\nimpl Default for VmSpace {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self::new()\n    }\n}\n@rikosellic Shall we add a comment of the original code to infer that there is a convertion?\n\nWell, there could be two ways:\n\nConvert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.\nUse ExTrait and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.\n\nI chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for ExDefault that forbids us to declare another one",
      "body": "> So this is the convert of\r\n> \r\n> ```rust\r\n> impl Default for VmSpace {\r\n>     fn default() -> Self {\r\n>         Self::new()\r\n>     }\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> @rikosellic Shall we add a comment of the original code to infer that there is a convertion?\r\n\r\nWell, there could be two ways:\r\n\r\n- Convert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.\r\n- Use `ExTrait` and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.\r\n\r\nI chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for `ExDefault` that forbids us to declare another one",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
