      "created_at": "2026-05-13T02:09:48Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-05-13T02:09:48Z",
      "body_html": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Well, there could be two ways:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Convert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.</li>\n<li>Use <code class=\"notranslate\">ExTrait</code> and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for <code class=\"notranslate\">ExDefault</code> that forbids us to declare another one</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The conversion itself is not the problem.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What I meant is that we may want to add a comment documenting the original code pattern before conversion.<br>\nThis would make future upstream synchronization or rebasing easier, because we can quickly understand what the verified version was converted from.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example:<br>\n</p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/asterinas/vostd/blob/9c3832311ed0162b7022ea2d9ebebe351badffda/ostd/src/sync/rwlock.rs#L905-L913\">vostd/ostd/src/sync/rwlock.rs</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n        Lines 905 to 913\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/asterinas/vostd/commit/9c3832311ed0162b7022ea2d9ebebe351badffda\">9c38323</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L905\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"905\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC905\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\">impl&lt;T: ?Sized, G: SpinGuardian&gt; Drop for RwLockWriteGuard&lt;'_, T, G&gt; {</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L906\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"906\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC906\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\">    fn drop(&amp;mut self) {</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L907\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"907\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC907\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\">        self.inner.lock.fetch_and(!WRITER, Release);</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L908\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"908\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC908\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\">    }</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L909\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"909\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC909\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\">}*/</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L910\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"910\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC910\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\">  </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L911\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"911\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC911\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-k\">impl</span>&lt;<span class=\"pl-v\">T</span>  <span class=\"pl-c\">/*: ?Sized*/</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">G</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">SpinGuardian</span>&gt; <span class=\"pl-v\">RwLockWriteGuard</span>&lt;<span class=\"pl-c1\">'</span>_<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">T</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">G</span>&gt; <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L912\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"912\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC912\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\">     <span class=\"pl-c\">/// VERUS LIMITATION: We implement `drop` and call it manually because Verus's support for `Drop` is incomplete for now.</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L913\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"913\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC913\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-c\"></span>    <span class=\"pl-k\">pub</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> drop<span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p></p>",
      "body_text": "Well, there could be two ways:\n\nConvert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.\nUse ExTrait and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.\n\nI chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for ExDefault that forbids us to declare another one\n\nThe conversion itself is not the problem.\nWhat I meant is that we may want to add a comment documenting the original code pattern before conversion.\nThis would make future upstream synchronization or rebasing easier, because we can quickly understand what the verified version was converted from.\nFor example:\n\n  \n    \n      vostd/ostd/src/sync/rwlock.rs\n    \n    \n        Lines 905 to 913\n      in\n      9c38323\n    \n  \n  \n    \n\n        \n          \n           impl<T: ?Sized, G: SpinGuardian> Drop for RwLockWriteGuard<'_, T, G> { \n        \n\n        \n          \n               fn drop(&mut self) { \n        \n\n        \n          \n                   self.inner.lock.fetch_and(!WRITER, Release); \n        \n\n        \n          \n               } \n        \n\n        \n          \n           }*/ \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n        \n\n        \n          \n           impl<T  /*: ?Sized*/ , G: SpinGuardian> RwLockWriteGuard<'_, T, G> { \n        \n\n        \n          \n               /// VERUS LIMITATION: We implement `drop` and call it manually because Verus's support for `Drop` is incomplete for now. \n        \n\n        \n          \n               pub fn drop(self) {",
      "body": "> Well, there could be two ways:\r\n> \r\n> * Convert unsupported traits into member functions but this requires some code changes.\r\n> * Use `ExTrait` and add a spec impl glue so that we can specify preconditions/postconditions but this might not be general for all cases and sometimes unstraightforward.\r\n> \r\n> I chose to avoid the second one since sometimes Verus has a spec layer for `ExDefault` that forbids us to declare another one\r\n\r\nThe conversion itself is not the problem. \r\n\r\nWhat I meant is that we may want to add a comment documenting the original code pattern before conversion. \r\nThis would make future upstream synchronization or rebasing easier, because we can quickly understand what the verified version was converted from.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\nhttps://github.com/asterinas/vostd/blob/9c3832311ed0162b7022ea2d9ebebe351badffda/ostd/src/sync/rwlock.rs#L905-L913",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
